{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1073108-what-of-the-daredevils","id":1073108,"title":"What of the Daredevils?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-04T07:26:20-07:00","id":1073108,"title":"What of the Daredevils?","content":"In Adventure!, there are 3 types of Inspired... Daredevils, Mesmerists and Stalwarts.<br /> <br /> \u200bWe know that in Aberrant that the Stalwarts are the precursors to that era's Novas.<br /> <br /> We know that in Trinity (Aeon) that the Mesmerists are the precursors to that era's Psions.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut what happens to the Daredevils as time progresses? These are still exceptional individuals of extraordinary skill. True, they may not longer be on the scale of Novas or Psions when those two inherit the full scope of their abilities... but Daredevils are still head and shoulders above the average person.<br /> <br /> \u200bWill there be an era where the Daredevils get their time to shine... when neither Nova nor Psion will overshadow their contribution to the human race? How do such individuals survive and compete in a world where their extraordinary skills and abilities seem like mere parlor tricks to Novas or Psions that clearly outmatch them.<br /> <br /> Is there a place for the Daredevil after Adventure!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T07:38:31-07:00","id":1073116,"title":"","content":"I believe that all three are present in all Eras, but each Era has their &quot;main&quot; Inspired. The Daredevil's time *is* Adventure!. <br /> <br /> Depending on what they do with the Norca re-creation of the Hammersmith experiment, they might be making a comeback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T07:42:05-07:00","id":1073118,"title":"","content":"Actually, the Daredevil's time is the Trinity Continuum's core book, which will feature a modern-day setting populated by Talents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T08:56:47-07:00","id":1073156,"title":"","content":"From what I've read (in the PDFs I have and other threads here)... there may also be another time when Daredevils (or whatever they will be called after Adventure!) will become more influential... during the time of the Crash... after the Aberrants are forced off of Earth and before the rise of the Psion Orders... roughly from 2061 to about 2103... roughly 40 years when neither Aberrants nor Psions have much influence on humanity... thus it seems likely that it will fall to the Daredevils to guide their fellow man through this turbulent time.<br /> <br /> \u200bBeyond this... who knows what the future will hold for any of these three groups. It is possible... even likely that they have appeared many times in the past... and will continue to do so into the far future. It seems that the timeline of Trinity has cycles where one or more of these groups rise to influence humanity in some way. Adventure! seems to be one of the few times all three have risen to roughly the same levels of power... though it is possible that there have been other times... especially if Michael Donighal's other designations for these three are somewhat accurate (Heroes, Wizards and Gods).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T09:35:11-07:00","id":1073186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1073108-what-of-the-daredevils#post1073108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Adventure!, there are 3 types of Inspired... Daredevils, Mesmerists and Stalwarts.<br /> <br /> \u200bWe know that in Aberrant that the Stalwarts are the precursors to that era's Novas.<br /> <br /> We know that in Trinity (Aeon) that the Mesmerists are the precursors to that era's Psions.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut what happens to the Daredevils as time progresses? These are still exceptional individuals of extraordinary skill. True, they may not longer be on the scale of Novas or Psions when those two inherit the full scope of their abilities... but Daredevils are still head and shoulders above the average person.<br /> <br /> \u200bWill there be an era where the Daredevils get their time to shine... when neither Nova nor Psion will overshadow their contribution to the human race? How do such individuals survive and compete in a world where their extraordinary skills and abilities seem like mere parlor tricks to Novas or Psions that clearly outmatch them.<br /> <br /> Is there a place for the Daredevil after Adventure!?</div> </div> </div> </div>As featured in the last few <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/187947?affiliate_id=13&amp;src=TheOnyxPath\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path brochures</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brochure</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Every Age Has Its Heroes.</b><br /> <br /> Our modern world is fraught with dangers, from the products of mad science and corporate greed to the perils of lost civilizations. Fortunately, as many of the Talented will tell you, danger is their middle name, and the \u00c6on Society is here to help them put things to right. The only constant in the world is change, and that\u2019s where you come in.<br /> <br /> At long last, the Trinity Continuum returns in this new edition with a new system and setting revised from the ground up. Talents: the subtle champions, daredevils of unparalleled skill and luck. Psiads: those able to employ the powers of their own minds to affect those around them. Novas: the stalwart few with the power to alter the very fabric of reality.<br /> <br /> These Inspired arise in times of need. Few of them will ever sit idly: they seem to be driven to act. Some will be crowned as heroes, others as power\u2013mad aberrations. Which will you be?<br /> <br /> The <b>Trinity Continuum Rulebook </b>will include:<ul><li>The Storypath system</li> <li>A modern introductory setting that\u2019s packed with action and adventure</li> <li>A full guide to playing Talents, their Gifts, and their various allegiances.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>The TC core covers Talents, the modern name for daredevils. Insofar as daredevils have an era of their own, it's the modern-day setting of the TC core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T12:30:38-07:00","id":1073305,"title":"","content":"is there any word for when Aberrant will happen for the superpowers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T17:07:09-07:00","id":1073438,"title":"","content":"After Aeon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T19:13:40-07:00","id":1073496,"title":"","content":"Currently I'm wondering how these are going to fit in with the proposed Aegis and Anima. Aegis could probably be simply Novas again, but I'm not sure which type works best for Anima.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T19:14:52-07:00","id":1073498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1073108-what-of-the-daredevils?p=1073305#post1073305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is there any word for when Aberrant will happen for the superpowers?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hopeful for early 2019.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T19:34:49-07:00","id":1073507,"title":"","content":"Is Anima the one in the aftermath of the Aberrant War? IIRC, it's another Talents setting: after the Aberrants took their leave, but before the rise of the Psion Orders. Basically, as close as the Trinity Continuum is likely to get to \u201chard Sci-fi\u201d.<br /> <br /> I suspect that \u00c6gis will be biased toward Eximorphs; but I won't be surprised to see psychomorphs there in the guise of magicians. Of the three types, they've always been the most compatible with a mystical outlook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T19:42:56-07:00","id":1073512,"title":"","content":"Okay... I know Anima takes place between Aberrant and Aeon(Trinity)... but I am not familiar with Aegis... where in the timeline will this be?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">\u200bOkay... so I'm not as fully caught up with all the little details as I would like to think.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T20:28:29-07:00","id":1073534,"title":"","content":"Aegis should be about bronze age, greco-romany thingies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T05:13:56-07:00","id":1073674,"title":"","content":"That would make sense... they had powerful God-like beings (Novas), great Heroes (Daredevils)... but I don't recall many wizard types (Psions)... but then it has been some time since I bushed up on my mythology of that era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T10:45:06-07:00","id":1073796,"title":"","content":"Adventure!, page 27:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doctor Primoris</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we can look to myth and legend for a different way to categorize the new breed walking the earth, should categories be desired. Daredevils are the heroes of myth, the Daedaluses as well as the Jasons. Mesmerists are the wizards, witches and sorcerers who haunt the corners of our past. And stalwarts? Stalwarts are gods. Gods of the dawning age.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T18:40:29-07:00","id":1073961,"title":"","content":"Heh. Sounds an awful lot like Scion. It's not, of course; Dr. Primoris' opinion to the contrary, Novas are not gods. Though they may sometimes play them on TV\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T22:48:23-07:00","id":1074024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1073108-what-of-the-daredevils?p=1073961#post1073961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh. Sounds an awful lot like Scion. It's not, of course; Dr. Primoris' opinion to the contrary, Novas are not gods. Though they may sometimes play them on TV\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When you can create yourown universe you can call yourself a god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T03:33:58-07:00","id":1074073,"title":"","content":"What makes a God a God?<br /> <br /> \u200bIf Novas have God-like powers and can perform acts that are miraculous... then by that standard, a Nova is a God. If Novas have appeared time and time again throughout human history... who's to say that the Gods of the past were not merely Novas? Does that make them any less of a God? True, less advanced cultures wouldn't understand how such beings accomplish such miraculous feats... but then does knowing how such feats are done make them any less of a miracle? Even in the setting... while people have an idea of what is being done... the how and why it can be done is still not completely understood.<br /> <br /> \u200bJust because we have a better understanding of what is going on in the setting doesn't mean that Novas aren't Gods. If something looks like a duck, swims like a duck and quacks like a duck... then chances are that it is a duck. Novas can do anything the ancient Gods were capable of... they can throw lightning bolts, create storms, move faster than almost anything, lift amazing weights. Because of Taint...many Novas develop inhuman features much like many Gods were depicted to have. Many Novas have even become the focus of cults and worship. If a Nova can do the things that Gods were capable of... look in ways remnant of the way Gods looked... and people choose to worship them as Gods... then for all intents and purposes... they are effectively Gods.<br /> <br /> \u200bAll this said, the Gods were also arrogant, spiteful and even petty at times... not unlike many Novas become over time. True, some Gods still tried to act in ways that many would feel was worthy of Gods... protecting and even encouraging growth amongst mortals... not unlike the few Novas that try not to abuse their powers. Other Gods reveled in their powers and their ability to cause strife and destruction... and were often confronted by those who tried to maintain a proper order and balance... not unlike what is said to have happened in the Aberrant War... with many Novas causing strife... and others trying to stop them. If most pantheons of Gods had good and evil Gods amongst them... like the Novas of various nations and organizations do... then really what is the difference?<br /> <br /> \u200bNone. A God by any other name is still a Nova. Everything else is mere semantics.<br /> <br /> \u200bAt least in this setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T13:45:29-07:00","id":1074304,"title":"","content":"You'll note that I referenced Scion in my post. Implicit was that its gods provide the yardstick as to what a god is. The typical Nova isn't anywhere close to a god; he's more of a demigod.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T18:14:30-07:00","id":1074436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1073108-what-of-the-daredevils?p=1074304#post1074304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll note that I referenced Scion in my post. Implicit was that its gods provide the yardstick as to what a god is. The typical Nova isn't anywhere close to a god; he's more of a demigod.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A quantum 1 Nova isn't particularly goddy but neither is a legend 1 Scion a Quantum 10 Nova on the otherhand... well perhaps we need new words for such a creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T22:45:20-07:00","id":1074525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1073108-what-of-the-daredevils?p=1074304#post1074304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll note that I referenced Scion in my post. Implicit was that its gods provide the yardstick as to what a god is. The typical Nova isn't anywhere close to a god; he's more of a demigod.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apples to Oranges.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe two game-lines operate on completely different premises.<br /> <br /> Trinity operates on the assumption that the Gods, Wizards and Heroes of the past were merely versions of the Novas, Psions and Daredevils of the present (and future).<br /> <br /> Scion operates on the assumption that the Gods have always existed and the exceptional beings of legend and myth are their offspring.<br /> <br /> \u200bYou really can't compare the two to each other as they are set in worlds that can't really be compared. In Scion, chances are that a Nova may get slapped around by the Gods because he has no divine blood with which to harm them. By the reverse, a God in the Trinity Universe may get their ass handed to them by a Nova because that divine blood means nothing in that universe. It is like trying to compare Vampires to Abyssals or Changeling: the Lost to Changeling: The Dreaming... the different universes they operate within are very different from each other.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs far as the Trinity is concerned... the difference between a God of the past and the Novas of today are practically non-existent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T21:51:56-07:00","id":1075366,"title":"","content":"I personally feel like power isn't the only thing that defines a god. I feel that a god also has to be some kind of essential element to nature or reality as well. Like, if you have a nova who can throw lightning bolts and summon rain and ride the wind she might very well be easy enough to call a God of Storms, but she isn't really the true personification of storms - she doesn't directly guide storms everywhere, storms still happen without her direct will, storms did not start happening because of her direct will, and if she ceases to be the phenomenon she controls or exemplifies will not be hurt or diminished in any real way.<br /> <br /> Now if we are talking about something like say, Universe Creation, where the nova creator might very well be tied directly such that their will and well being is tied to the reality they created, then you might have a good chance at godhood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T04:49:43-07:00","id":1075434,"title":"","content":"When a Nova can bend the very laws of reality in ways that most can not understand... I would say they are connected on some fundamental level to the very universe.<br /> <br /> \u200bwhen it comes down to it... it is mere semantics whether or not Nova's can be considered Gods or not... for in the end... who is really going to argue with a being that can smite you for saying otherwise... God or not? If you did the same thing to a &quot;real&quot; God... the result would still be the same. So in the end... real or not... what Novas choose to be called doesn't matter... one isn't likely to survive making one of them angry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T13:35:54-07:00","id":1075576,"title":"","content":"There are degrees, which is why I tend to think of Novas as being more akin to demigods than gods for the most part: most Novas aren't in the same tier as, say, Dr. Manhattan. I wouldn't call, say, Wolverine or Plastic Man gods. <br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm curious whether there will be a setting with \u201cpowered up\u201d Talents, where they gain a <i>conscious</i> ability to manipulate and traverse the Continuum. Or is Max Mercer going to remain unique in that regard?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T15:08:48-07:00","id":1075595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1073108-what-of-the-daredevils?p=1075434#post1075434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> who is really going to argue with a being that can smite you for saying otherwise... God or not? If you did the same thing to a &quot;real&quot; God... the result would still be the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>By that logic the American President is a god.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T17:36:04-07:00","id":1075646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1073108-what-of-the-daredevils?p=1075595#post1075595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By that logic the American President is a god.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHardly... and with the recent President... EVERYONE has been criticizing his power and the way he exercises it. So far no one has been smited or even made to &quot;disappear&quot; because of their vocal opinions of him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T23:45:01-07:00","id":1075755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1073108-what-of-the-daredevils?p=1075576#post1075576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I'm curious whether there will be a setting with \u201cpowered up\u201d Talents, where they gain a <i>conscious</i> ability to manipulate and traverse the Continuum. Or is Max Mercer going to remain unique in that regard?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ian's mentioned that while Max may be unique for the duration of the detailed Continuum, he's got plans for detailing how Talent PCs could potentially reach Max's level of power - not in the core, but somewhere along the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T05:05:23-07:00","id":1075842,"title":"","content":"It does seem that Daredevils/Talented are getting the short end of the stick compared to Stalwarts/Novas and Mesmerists/Psions. True, the Talented are unlikely to do the obviously impossible feats that Novas or Psions can... but that doesn't mean that they are any weaker than these groups. It may take some creative use or combination of Talents to deal with the paranormal powers the higher end Novas or Psions can perform... but then it is a challenge that many Talented would accept.<br /> <br /> I would say that Batman would be an ultimate example of a Talented-type character... and many of the rogues in his gallery would have Nova or Psion-like abilities. While they are arguably more powerful than him, he is more than capable of dealing with such abilities with the skills and gadgets he has access to. He's even taken on high end Nova-like characters and come out on top.<br /> <br /> \u200bHopefully there will be Talents and such to help span the power-gap that it seems that the Talented fell behind when Novas and Psions came into their own in Aberrant and Trinity (Aeon).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T06:16:47-07:00","id":1075853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1073108-what-of-the-daredevils?p=1075842#post1075842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bHopefully there will be Talents and such to help span the power-gap that it seems that the Talented fell behind when Novas and Psions came into their own in Aberrant and Trinity (Aeon).</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm. Ian's view of how Talents work is that they have discrete energy plateaus. Most Talents are at the first plateau, where they seem to be lucky or skilled. Max got a <i>massive</i> amount of energy in the Hammersmith Event, catapaulting him to the next plateau.<br /> <br /> Which is to say Talents leap from 'born lucky' to 'time travellers' without much in-between.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T15:12:38-07:00","id":1076138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1073108-what-of-the-daredevils?p=1075646#post1075646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bHardly... and with the recent President... EVERYONE has been criticizing his power and the way he exercises it. So far no one has been smited or even made to &quot;disappear&quot; because of their vocal opinions of him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lack of will does not necessarily indicate lack of ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T15:17:10-07:00","id":1076143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1073108-what-of-the-daredevils?p=1075842#post1075842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does seem that Daredevils/Talented are getting the short end of the stick compared to Stalwarts/Novas and Mesmerists/Psions. True, the Talented are unlikely to do the obviously impossible feats that Novas or Psions can... but that doesn't mean that they are any weaker than these groups. It may take some creative use or combination of Talents to deal with the paranormal powers the higher end Novas or Psions can perform... but then it is a challenge that many Talented would accept.<br /> <br /> I would say that Batman would be an ultimate example of a Talented-type character... and many of the rogues in his gallery would have Nova or Psion-like abilities. While they are arguably more powerful than him, he is more than capable of dealing with such abilities with the skills and gadgets he has access to. He's even taken on high end Nova-like characters and come out on top.<br /> <br /> \u200bHopefully there will be Talents and such to help span the power-gap that it seems that the Talented fell behind when Novas and Psions came into their own in Aberrant and Trinity (Aeon).</div> </div> </div> </div>Batman tends to be helped by having a lot of his enemies fight him in a stupid manner. That's probably the power that really starts to differentiate the merely lucky from the truly great.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T21:08:41-07:00","id":1076276,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I don't expect a Talented character to be able to go blow for blow against a Nova... or even a Psion... at least not Talent vs. Power vs. Psionics... but I also don't expect a Nova or Psion to be able to wipe the floor with a Talented character of equivalent experience. Balanced doesn't always mean equal... merely equivalent.<br /> <br /> \u200bWith the right selection of Talents, a Talented character should be a challenge to even a Nova of equivalent ability... say both as starting characters... or both with an equal amount of experience under their belts. Yes, their abilities will be different... and a Nova may have a few abilities that are at a higher plateau than the Talents the Talented Character has... but those will cost more to develop... balancing the power with the greater number of Talents a Talented character will have for the same cost.<br /> <br /> \u200bThis is often how Batman goes up against more powerful villains that clearly have powers that he can't easily match. He may not be able to match the shape-shifting powers of Clayface, but he has the intelligence and resources to develop the means to overcome that advantage. Even opponents as powerful as Superman can be overcome by Batman with his tactical thinking, resources to get rare materials that can harm such individuals and a little planning... something Talented characters are more likely to rely upon than flashy powers.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy point is that if a player chooses to play one of the Talented, he shouldn't feel that he is completely helpless when dealing with a Nova or even a Psion... and they shouldn't think that a Talented character is a mere Extra that can be dealt with without any worry.<br /> <br /> \u200bThose who underestimate the Batman quickly come to regret that choice... and the same should be true for any Nova or Psion that underestimates the tenacity of a Talented character.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:09:03-07:00","id":1077459,"title":"","content":"I would say I prefer distinct &quot;tiers&quot; of power. I don't need everybody balanced with other types; it's hard enough to balance within it's own type.<br /> <br /> Batman can take Clayface, but Batman is probably a high level Talent, if not the highest you can get without rolling over into something else entirely, and Clayface would be a fairly shitty nova. Really, he's more a challenge to Batman's detective abilities than anything else. Superman is a better example, but note most Batman V. Superman conflicts are heavily affected by environment and situation - Superman, even when written as the &quot;bad guy&quot; in the scenario, almost always lets his opponent dictate the terms of the engagement. You don't need &quot;tactical genius&quot; if your opponent is already going to let you pick the battle ground. <br /> <br /> That is one of the harder things about so-called balance in a role-playing game - you can't always account for situations. Environment changes things. Equipment changes things. Allies change things. Innocents change things. A man is infinitely smarter and more powerful than a spider, but a spider can kill someone under the right conditions.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like the idea that a high end Talent is equivalent roughly to a low end nova (Batman v Clayface) and can beat a mid to mid-upper level nova if they are lucky and the situation favors them (Batman v Superman). Discussing where psions fall into it I think is getting into whether Batman can beat Darth Vader.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}